es\nSubsidized Health Insurance\nGrants, Fellowships, and Awards\nInternal Funding Resources\nDissertation Completion Grants\nHigh Impact Grants\nDoctoral Research Scholars\nSummer Research Assistantship\nExternal Funding Resources\nGraduate Fellowships\nFunding Search Tools\nResources and Advice\nFinancial Aid and Loans\nConference Travel Funding\nHow to Apply\nTravel Research Incentive Program (T.R.I.P.)\nTuition\nGraduate Funding FAQs\nProfessional Development\nIndividual Development Plan\nCareer Planning\nAcademic Career Planning Resources\nAccelerate to Industry (A2i)\nPreparing for Careers in the Academy\nResearch Skills and Opportunities\nTeaching Skills\nAnnual Conferences at Mason\nMason Graduate Interdisciplinary Conference\nCommunication Skills and Publication\nCommunication Academy\nLeadership and Community Engagement\nFaculty & Staff\nGraduate Council\nGraduate Program Directors and Coordinators\nGraduate Admission\nGraduate Faculty Status\nGraduate Student Hiring\nGraduate Student Hiring Rules & Procedures\nMentoring\nPresidential Scholarship\nTeaching and Curriculum Resources\nAbout\nGraduate Division History\nMeet Our Team\nMeet the Graduate Division Team\nMeet the Graduate Student Life Team\nMeet the Office of Fellowships's Graduate Fellowships Staff\nContact\nEvents\nGraduate Student Weekly Newsletter\nApply\nGive\nCanvas\nPatriotWeb\nPeoplefinder\nAthletics\nNews\nCALENDAR\nLibrary\nGraduation\nGraduate Education\nProspective Students\nSub Navigation\nProspective Students\nNewly Admitted Students\nInternational Graduate Students\nGraduate Student Policy Resources\nGraduate Student Resources\nGraduate Success Fellows\nStart Your Journey at George Mason\nYou'll make a great investment in yourself by pursuing an advanced degree here.\nAbout Applying to Graduate School at George Mason\nGeorge Mason University is the largest Research 1 and public university in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Our goal is to support individuals on their academic journey at an affordable rate.\nGeorge Mason graduate programs are competitive, each with their own admission requirements, application processes, and deadlines;\nFactors that weigh into your selection are based on the strength of your academic background, results of standardized exams (if required by the program), work experience, and any additional evidence of potential success in the program.\nAll applicants for graduate study at George Mason University must meet the admission standards specified in theGraduate Admission Policieschapter of the University Catalog.\nReady to apply? Get started with the Office of Graduate Admissions\nGraduate Programs Offered at George Mason:\nGeorge Mason offers over 130 graduate-level degree programs and over 100 graduate-level certificates. Explore the option that best suits your needs and goals.\nYou can do this through reviewing the program-specific information, attending an information session, and contacting academic programs for further information.\nMosaic tile\nMaster's\nMosaic tile\nDoctoral\nMosaic tile\nGraduate Certificate\nMosaic tile\nBachelor's/Accelerated Master's\nLocate Your Program Application Deadlines and Requirements\nTimelines and admission requirements vary across George Mason's schools and colleges. To locate your program's specific standards, navigate to your program using the provided links.\nThe Office of Fellowships offers helpful resource guides for compiling your materials for applying for a program, funding, fellowships and more.\nRequirements By College or School\nMosaic tile\nAntonin Scalia Law School\nMosaic tile\nCarter School for Peace and Conflict Resolution\nMosaic tile\nCollege of Education and Human Development\nMosaic tile\nCollege of Engineering and Computing\nMosaic tile\nCollege of Humanities and Social Sciences\nMosaic tile\nCollege of Public Health\nMosaic tile\nCollege of Science\nMosaic tile\nCollege of Visual and Performing Arts\nMosaic tile\nSchar School of Policy and Government\nMosaic tile\nCostello College of Business\nApplication Fees and Fee Waivers\nProspective graduate students must pay a non-refundable fee of $75 when submitting an application. Full-time George Mason faculty or classified staff and eligible Virginia residents, 60 years or older may be eligible for an application fee waiver\nApplication Status\nWhen you submit an application, you will receive a confirmation email. Check the application portal to confirm that George Mason has received all required documents. Applications will then be sent to the appropriate program and faculty for review. All decisions are released to applicants via the application portal.\nALL TOGETHER DIFFERENT\nGeorge Mason University\n4400 University Drive\nFairfax, Virginia 22030\nTel: +1(703) 993-1000\n\u00a9 2026 George Mason University\nSitemap\nSitemap\nContact\nTitle IX\nAccessibility\nJobs\nStudent Consumer Information\nPrivacy Statement\nFOIA\nALL TOGETHER DIFFERENT\nGeorge Mason University\n4400 University Drive\nFairfax, Virginia 22030\nTel: +1(703) 993-1000\n\u00a9 2026 George Mason University\nGraduate Education\nStudying Here\nProspective Students\nNewly Admitted Students\nInternational Graduate Students\nGraduate Student Policy Resources\nGraduate Student Resources\nGraduate Success Fellows\nAll-Inclusive\nGraduate Student Life\nResearch\nFinancial Support\nProfessional Development\nFaculty & Staff\nAbout\nApply\nGive\nCanvas\nPatriotWeb\nPeoplefinder\nAthletics\nNews\nCALENDAR\nLibrary\nGraduation", "links": [["Skip to content", "https://graduate.gmu.edu/studying-here/prospective-students#content"], ["", "https://graduate.gmu.edu/"], ["Graduate Education", "https://graduate.gmu.edu/"], ["Mason George Mason University", "https://www.gmu.edu"], ["Apply", "https://graduate.gmu.edu/admissions-aid"], ["Give", "https://graduate.gmu.edu/give"], ["Canvas", "https://canvas.gmu.edu/"], ["PatriotWeb", "https://patriotweb.gmu.edu/"], ["Peoplefinder", "https://peoplefinder.gmu.edu/"], ["Athletics", "https: